      <Tag Name="TMR_C_E_Delay" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          ONDTR TENTHS on Logic rung 11, GE register System_C_E_Delay %R00202, PV 1200 tenths = 120000 ms (120 s), R pin = #ALW_OFF %S00008 (never resets). Drives flag T00002 %T00002.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_DelugeFail" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          TON for the GE ONDTR TENTHS of CE_LOG rung 18 (retentive on-delay, cleared by the derived RES rung), GE timer register Pump_Timer7 %R00227, preset 600 tenths = 60000 ms (60 s); its done bit drives DelugeFailedToRelease %M00620.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_HMI_Reset" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          ONDTR TENTHS on Logic rung 5, GE register System_HMI_Reset_Timer %R00205, PV 50 tenths = 5000 ms (5 s), R pin = System_Reset_HMI_Help %M00704. Timer helper name used because the GE register is a WORD array, not a Logix TIMER.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_Pump_Timer10" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          ONDTR TENTHS on Protect rung 13 - GE timer register Pump_Timer10 %R00236 (WORD[3] in var.xml), PV 700 tenths = 70000 ms (70.0 s). Its .DN drives %M00295 PUMP_B_START_OC (open circuit).
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_Pump_Timer11" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          ONDTR TENTHS on Protect rung 7 - GE timer register Pump_Timer11 %R00239 (WORD[3] in var.xml), PV 280 tenths = 28000 ms (28.0 s). Its .DN drives %T00013.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_Pump_Timer12" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          ONDTR TENTHS on Protect rung 11 - GE timer register Pump_Timer12 %R00242 (WORD[3] in var.xml), PV 280 tenths = 28000 ms (28.0 s). Its .DN drives %T00014.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_Pump_Timer9" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          ONDTR TENTHS on Protect rung 9 - GE timer register Pump_Timer9 %R00233 (WORD[3] in var.xml), PV 700 tenths = 70000 ms (70.0 s). Its .DN drives %M00293 PUMP_A_OC (open circuit).
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_T00003" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          TON for GE ONDTR TENTHS %T00003 in CE_LOG rung 11 (ONDTR = retentive on-delay, accumulated value kept when the rung goes false; cleared by the derived RES rung), preset 300 tenths = 30000 ms (30 s), GE timer register Pump_Timer1 %R00209.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_T00004" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          TON for GE TMR TENTHS %T00004 in CE_LOG rung 12 (TMR = non-retentive on-delay), preset 20 tenths = 2000 ms (2 s), GE timer register Pump_Timer2 %R00212.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_T00005" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
          TON for GE TMR TENTHS %T00005 in CE_LOG rung 13 (non-retentive on-delay), preset 600 tenths = 60000 ms (60 s), GE timer register Pump_Timer3 %R00215.
        ]]>
        </Description>
      </Tag>
      <Tag Name="TMR_T00006" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER">
        <Description>
<![CDATA[
