    </Tags>
    <Programs>
      <Program Name="FandG_Angola" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="MainRoutine" Disabled="false">
        <Tags/>
        <Routines>
          <Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Main Routine: Master Cyclic Scan Dispatcher
Orchestrates the top-level cyclic execution sequence of the Fire & Gas safety application. Executes Init on power-up / first scan (S:FS), and continuously dispatches Input, Logic, Modbus_Comm, and Output routines during normal running scans.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Scan Power-Up Initialization: Interlocked with system first scan bit (S:FS). Executes subroutine 'Init' exactly once upon controller transition to RUN mode to initialize watchdog timers, clear accumulators, and unlatch acoustic alarms.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(S:FS)JSR(Init,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Cyclic Input Processing Dispatcher: Executed continuously on all normal scans (XIO S:FS). Calls subroutine 'Input' to map physical backplane I/O, apply digital de-bounce filtering, scale 4-20mA analog channels, and evaluate 1oo2/2oo3 voting.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(S:FS)JSR(Input,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Cyclic Safety Logic & Cause-and-Effect Dispatcher: Executed continuously on all normal scans (XIO S:FS). Calls subroutine 'Logic' to evaluate master System_Reset, clock pulse generators, detector warm-up delay timers, and trigger Cause & Effect matrix subroutine CE_LOG.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(S:FS)JSR(Logic,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Cyclic Modbus Serial Engine Communications: Executed continuously on all normal scans (XIO S:FS). Calls subroutine 'Modbus_Comm' to poll ProSoft MVI56E-MCM module (Slot 9) for Clarke / Murphy diesel pump engine data (RPM, oil pressure, coolant temperature, running hours).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(S:FS)JSR(Modbus_Comm,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Cyclic Safety Output & Physical Actuation Dispatcher: Executed continuously on all normal scans (XIO S:FS). Calls subroutine 'Output' to evaluate fail-safe ESD trips, pump safeguarding, panel LED indicators, local sirens, and write final commands to Slot 8 1756-OB32 physical outputs.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(S:FS)JSR(Output,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Init" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Init (Cold / Warm Startup Initialization)
Executes exclusively on the first program scan (S:FS). Clears pump pulse timer accumulators, resets Cause & Effect warm-up delays, unlatches acoustic alarms, and initializes internal flags to prevent spurious trips or uncommanded horn sounding during CPU boot.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Timer Accumulator Cold-Start Clear: Clears pump pulse timer accumulators (Pump_Timer1[0] = 0) and resets Cause & Effect delay timer (System_C_E_Delay[0] = 0) on CPU power-up to ensure predictable initial timing.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [MOV(0,Pump_Timer1[0]),MOV(0,System_C_E_Delay[0])];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Acoustic Alarm Internal Latches Power-Up Clear: Unlatches internal horn command (SA_7404_001_002_INT) and strobe beacon command (Tag_DO_15_INT). Prevents acoustic alarms from sounding immediately upon panel power restoration.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [OTU(Tag_DO_15_INT),OTU(SA_7404_001_002_INT)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump Pulse Watchdog Reset: Redundant zero-clear of electric pump A pulse timer to guarantee that no accidental start pulse is transmitted to the Motor Control Center (MCC) contactor upon CPU boot.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(0,Pump_Timer1[0]);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Input" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Input (Master Input Scan & Pre-Processing Dispatcher)
Sequences physical I/O mapping and conditioning routines in strict deterministic order: IO_Mapping_In -> DI_1 -> DI_2 -> AI_1 -> AI_2 -> AI_3 -> Vote_1.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Physical Input Buffer Mapping: Calls 'IO_Mapping_In' to copy raw input registers from Slot 7 1756-IB32 (Discrete Inputs), Slots 2-5 1756-IF16 (Analog Inputs), and Slot 6 1756-IF8H (HART Open Path) into internal tags.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(IO_Mapping_In,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Discrete Input Conditioning - Group 1: Calls 'DI_1' to condition valve position switches (6401-ZSH/ZSL-001), deluge flow switches (7503-FS-001), tank level switches (7503-LS-001/002), and panel pushbuttons.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(DI_1,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Discrete Input Conditioning - Group 2: Calls 'DI_2' to service future discrete field expansions and spare channels.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(DI_2,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Analog Combustible Gas Detectors - Group 1: Calls 'AI_1' to execute 4-20mA signal conditioning, NAMUR NE 43 checks, and alarm threshold evaluations for gas detectors 7404-DG-001 through 008 (Pump House & Skid).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(AI_1,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Analog Gas & Flame Detectors - Group 2: Calls 'AI_2' to process gas detectors 7404-DG-009/010, optical flame detectors 7404-DF-001/002, and open-path infrared gas detector 7404-DG-011R.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(AI_2,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Process Pressures & Deluge Foam Release: Calls 'AI_3' to process ESDV air pressure PST-7002-001, fuel gas header pressure PST-6401-001, deluge line pressure PST-7503-001, and foam release sensors FR-7503-001/002/003.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(AI_3,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Sensor Voting & Common Supervisory Fault Aggregation: Calls 'Vote_1' to execute 1oo2/2oo2 voting across gas zones, and aggregate all channel maintenance inhibits and hardware faults into supervisory tags.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(Vote_1,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="DI_1" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: DI_1 (Discrete Inputs Processing & Line Fault Monitoring - Group 1)
Conditions field discrete switches: ESD valve limit switches (6401-ZSH/ZSL-001), foam and firewater tank level switches (7503-LS-001/002), firewater deluge flow switch (7503-FS-001), pump run feedback pulses, manual ESD pushbuttons, and maintenance inhibit key-switches.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Shut-Off Valve Open Position (6401-ZSH-001): Reads limit switch High (TB-01: 01-02). XIC evaluates TRUE when the ESD valve is fully open, driving live status bit ZSH_6401_001_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ZSH_6401_001)OTE(ZSH_6401_001_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Valve Open Uninhibited Alarm: Passes valve open status to uninhibited alarm bit ZSH_6401_001_ALI for display on panel indicator lamp Tag_DO_12.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ZSH_6401_001_AL)OTE(ZSH_6401_001_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Shut-Off Valve Closed Position (6401-ZSL-001): Reads limit switch Low (TB-01: 03-04). XIC evaluates TRUE when the ESD valve is fully closed, driving live status bit ZSL_6401_001_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ZSL_6401_001)OTE(ZSL_6401_001_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Valve Closed Uninhibited Alarm: Passes valve closed status to uninhibited alarm bit ZSL_6401_001_ALI. Feeds panel door LED indicator Tag_DO_13.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ZSL_6401_001_AL)OTE(ZSL_6401_001_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Deluge Firewater Flow Switch (7503-FS-001): Reads flow switch contact (TB-01: 09-10). When firewater flows through the deluge valve, contact closes. Latches alarm FS_7503_001_AL until cleared by master System_Reset.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(FS_7503_001)XIO(System_Reset)OTE(FS_7503_001_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Deluge Firewater Flow Maintenance Inhibit: Passes latched flow alarm to active trip bit FS_7503_001_ALI unless suppressed by maintenance inhibit switch FS_7503_001_INH (e.g. during periodic deluge flow testing).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(FS_7503_001_AL)XIO(FS_7503_001_INH)OTE(FS_7503_001_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Firewater Storage Tank Low Level Switch (7503-LS-001): Reads low level float switch (TB-01: 11-12). Self-latches alarm LS_7503_001_AL upon low water level. Latched until water is replenished and System_Reset is pressed.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(LS_7503_001),XIC(LS_7503_001_AL)]XIO(System_Reset)OTE(LS_7503_001_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Firewater Tank Low Level Maintenance Inhibit: Passes latched low level alarm to active bit LS_7503_001_ALI unless masked by channel maintenance inhibit LS_7503_001_INH.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(LS_7503_001_AL)XIO(LS_7503_001_INH)OTE(LS_7503_001_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Foam Concentrate Tank Low Level Switch (7503-LS-002): Reads foam tank level switch (TB-01: 07-08). Self-latches alarm LS_7503_002_AL when AFFF foam concentrate falls below safety operating threshold.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(LS_7503_002),XIC(LS_7503_002_AL)]XIO(System_Reset)OTE(LS_7503_002_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Foam Tank Low Level Maintenance Inhibit: Passes latched foam low level alarm to active bit LS_7503_002_ALI unless masked by channel maintenance inhibit LS_7503_002_INH.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(LS_7503_002_AL)XIO(LS_7503_002_INH)OTE(LS_7503_002_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Fire Pump A Running Feedback Pulse: Reads auxiliary run feedback pulse from Pump A contactor (TB-01: 13-14). Drives internal run status bit Pump_A_PulsIn_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn)OTE(Pump_A_PulsIn_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Fire Pump A Run Uninhibited Status: Passes pump A run feedback to internal safety bit Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI. Resets the 70-second start failure watchdog timer in routine Protect.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_AL)OTE(Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Start Command Feedback Pulse: Reads start confirmation pulse from Diesel Pump B Murphy controller (TB-01: 15-16). Drives internal status bit Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn)OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Start Feedback Uninhibited: Passes start feedback to internal bit Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI. Resets the 70-second cranking failure watchdog timer in routine Protect.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_AL)OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Spare Digital Input Channel 08: Reads field contact (TB-01: 17-18). Reserved for expansion; drives SpareDI_08_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(SpareDI_08)OTE(SpareDI_08_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Spare Digital Input Channel 08 Uninhibited: Passes SpareDI_08_AL to SpareDI_08_ALI.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(SpareDI_08_AL)OTE(SpareDI_08_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Maintenance Inhibit Key-Switch: Reads panel door inhibit switch (TB-01: 17-18). When active, indicates standby diesel pump B is locked out for engine maintenance. Drives Pump_B_Inhibited_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited)OTE(Pump_B_Inhibited_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="17" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Inhibit Uninhibited Flag: Passes Pump_B_Inhibited_AL to active safety tag Pump_B_Inhibited_ALI. Prevents automatic cranking of Pump B during maintenance.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_AL)OTE(Pump_B_Inhibited_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="18" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Field Emergency Shutdown Pushbutton (6401-ESDV-001): Physically wired NORMALLY CLOSED (NC) for fail-safe integrity (TB-01: 25-26). In healthy normal state, 24VDC is present and contact is closed (1). When pressed or wire broken, contact opens (0). XIO evaluates TRUE on open contact, instantly latching emergency shutdown alarm ESDV_6401_001_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(ESDV_6401_001)OTE(ESDV_6401_001_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="19" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Field ESD Pushbutton Uninhibited Trip: Passes emergency pushbutton alarm to active trip bit ESDV_6401_001_ALI. Directly initiates immediate plant shutdown in Cause & Effect routine CE_LOG.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ESDV_6401_001_AL)OTE(ESDV_6401_001_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="20" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Spare Digital Input Channel 11: Reads field contact (TB-01: 21-22). Self-latches until System_Reset.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(SpareDI_11),XIC(SpareDI_11_AL)]XIO(System_Reset)OTE(SpareDI_11_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="21" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Spare Digital Input Channel 11 Inhibit: Masks SpareDI_11_AL with channel inhibit SpareDI_11_INH.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(SpareDI_11_AL)XIO(SpareDI_11_INH)OTE(SpareDI_11_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="22" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Foam Deluge Release Master Inhibit Key-Switch: Reads panel front key-switch (TB-01: 27-28). When engaged by authorized personnel, latches INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL until System_Reset.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL)XIO(System_Reset)OTE(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="23" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Foam Deluge Inhibit Active Flag: Passes INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL to active inhibit tag INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI. Interlocks deluge pump starting and solenoid discharge to prevent accidental foam release during dry testing.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_AL)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_INH)OTE(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="24" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[System Master Output Inhibit Key-Switch: Reads master key-switch (TB-01: 29-30). Used during panel commissioning to isolate all physical outputs. Latches INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS)XIO(System_Reset)OTE(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="25" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[System Master Output Inhibit Active Flag: Passes to INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI. Interlocks all 32 physical outputs to prevent accidental field trips while technicians perform live testing.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_AL)XIO(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_INH)OTE(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="DI_2" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: DI_2 (Discrete Inputs Processing - Group 2 / Spares)
Allocated for future field discrete expansion channels and secondary area monitoring.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Digital Inputs Expansion Group 2: Empty placeholder routine preserved from original GE Fanuc program structure. Reserved for future discrete I/O expansion.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  NOP();
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="AI_1" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: AI_1 (Analog Combustible Gas Detectors 7404-DG-001 to 008)
Processes 4-20mA combustible hydrocarbon gas detectors located in the Pump House and Fuel Gas Skid. Scales 0-100% LEL, evaluates Low Alarm (20% LEL), High Alarm (30% LEL), NAMUR NE 43 broken wire / open circuit (-10.0% / <3.6mA), and short circuit (98.0% / >21mA).]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Combustible Gas Detector 7404-DG-001 Parameter Setup & AOI Call: Located at Pump House North (TB-02: 1-3). Passes live 4-20mA signal DG_7404_001 (0-100% LEL). Configures setpoints: Low Alarm = 20.0% LEL, High Alarm = 30.0% LEL, NAMUR NE 43 Broken Wire / Open Circuit = -10.0% (<3.6mA / 400 counts), Short Circuit = 98.0% (>21mA). Enables low and high alarms with latching; passes channel inhibit DG_7404_001_INH and master System_Reset. Executes Add-On Instruction AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(DG_7404_001,AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.PV)MOV(20.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.LoAlarmSP)MOV(30.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.LoFaultSP)MOV(98.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.LoAlarmLE),OTL(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.HasHiAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.HasFaultWin),XIC(DG_7404_001_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[7404-DG-001 Output Unpacking: Maps AOI instance outputs to global tags: Val -> DG_7404_001_VAL (0-100% LEL for HMI display), ALL -> DG_7404_001_ALL (Latched 20% Low Alarm), ALLI -> DG_7404_001_ALLI (Uninhibited Low Alarm for amber flashing beacon), ALH -> DG_7404_001_ALH (Latched 30% High Alarm), ALHI -> DG_7404_001_ALHI (Uninhibited High Alarm for C&E ESD trip), FRUP -> DG_7404_001_FRUP (First-Out chronological trap), OC -> DG_7404_001_OC (3s debounced Open Circuit fault), SC -> DG_7404_001_SC (3s debounced Short Circuit fault).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.Val,DG_7404_001_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.ALL)OTE(DG_7404_001_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.ALLI)OTE(DG_7404_001_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.ALH)OTE(DG_7404_001_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.ALHI)OTE(DG_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.FRUP)OTE(DG_7404_001_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.OC)OTE(DG_7404_001_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_DG_7404_001.SC)OTE(DG_7404_001_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Combustible Gas Detector 7404-DG-002 Parameter Setup & AOI Call: Located at Pump House South (TB-02: 4-6). Scaled 0-100% LEL. Sets Low Alarm = 20.0% LEL, High Alarm = 30.0% LEL, Open Circuit = -10.0%, Short Circuit = 98.0%. Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(DG_7404_002,AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.PV)MOV(20.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.LoAlarmSP)MOV(30.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.LoFaultSP)MOV(98.0,AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.LoAlarmLE),OTL(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.HasHiAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.HasFaultWin),XIC(DG_7404_002_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_DG_7404_002);
                ]]>
