          <Routine Name="AI_3" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: AI_3 (Process Pressure Transmitters & Foam Deluge Release Monitors)
Monitors ESDV pneumatic air accumulator pressure PST-7002-001 (low-acting trip at 50 PSI), fuel gas header pressure PST-6401-001 (high trip at 100 PSI), deluge water pressure PST-7503-001, and foam release pressure transmitters FR-7503-001/002/003.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Pneumatic Air Accumulator Pressure (7002-PST-001): Located at ESD Valve Skid (TB-03: 13-14). Scaled 0-100 PSI (0-7 bar). Configured LOW-ACTING (LoAlarmLE = 1): trips when air pressure falls below LoAlarmSP = 50.0 PSI. If air pressure drops, the emergency shut-off valve cannot actuate. High alarm disabled (HasHiAlarm=0). Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(PST_7002_001,AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.PV)MOV(50.0,AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.LoAlarmSP)MOV(0.0,AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.LoFaultSP)MOV(98.0,AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.HiFaultSP)[OTL(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.LoAlarmLE),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.HasLoAlarm),OTU(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.HasHiAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.HasFaultWin),XIC(PST_7002_001_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[7002-PST-001 Output Unpacking: Maps outputs to PST_7002_001_VAL, _ALL, _ALLI, _ALH, _ALHI, _FRUP, _OC, _SC. ALLI drives panel door low air warning lamp Tag_DO_14.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.Val,PST_7002_001_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.ALL)OTE(PST_7002_001_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.ALLI)OTE(PST_7002_001_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.ALH)OTE(PST_7002_001_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.ALHI)OTE(PST_7002_001_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.FRUP)OTE(PST_7002_001_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.OC)OTE(PST_7002_001_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7002_001.SC)OTE(PST_7002_001_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Header Pressure Transmitter (6401-PST-001): Located at Fuel Gas Line (TB-03: 16-17). Scaled 0-150 PSI. High Alarm setpoint = 100.0 PSI. Low Alarm disabled (LoAlarmSP = 400.0). Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(PST_6401_001,AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.PV)MOV(400.0,AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.LoAlarmSP)MOV(100.0,AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-17.0,AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.LoFaultSP)MOV(147.0,AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.LoAlarmLE),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.HasHiAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.HasFaultWin),XIC(PST_6401_001_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[6401-PST-001 Output Unpacking: Maps outputs to PST_6401_001_VAL, _ALL, _ALLI, _ALH, _ALHI, _FRUP, _OC, _SC. ALHI initiates fuel gas valve isolation EY_6401_001_002.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.Val,PST_6401_001_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.ALL)OTE(PST_6401_001_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.ALLI)OTE(PST_6401_001_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.ALH)OTE(PST_6401_001_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.ALHI)OTE(PST_6401_001_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.FRUP)OTE(PST_6401_001_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.OC)OTE(PST_6401_001_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_6401_001.SC)OTE(PST_6401_001_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Deluge Firewater Line Pressure Transmitter (7503-PST-001): Located at Deluge Distribution Line (TB-03: 10-11). Scaled 0-16 bar (0-230 PSI). High Alarm setpoint = 50.0 PSI (confirms active deluge water discharge). Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(PST_7503_001,AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.PV)MOV(400.0,AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.LoAlarmSP)MOV(50.0,AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.LoFaultSP)MOV(102.0,AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.LoAlarmLE),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.HasHiAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.HasFaultWin),XIC(PST_7503_001_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[7503-PST-001 Output Unpacking: Maps outputs to PST_7503_001_VAL, _ALL, _ALLI, _ALH, _ALHI, _FRUP, _OC, _SC. ALHI confirms successful deluge release and resets the 30-second diesel pump standby start timer.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.Val,PST_7503_001_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.ALL)OTE(PST_7503_001_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.ALLI)OTE(PST_7503_001_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.ALH)OTE(PST_7503_001_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.ALHI)OTE(PST_7503_001_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.FRUP)OTE(PST_7503_001_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.OC)OTE(PST_7503_001_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_PST_7503_001.SC)OTE(PST_7503_001_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Foam Deluge Release Outside Local CP (7503-FR-001/002): Discharge pressure sensor outside control room (TB-03: 20). High Alarm = 30.0 PSI. Low Alarm disabled (LoAlarmSP = 400.0). Interlocked with deluge flow and pump run timer. Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(FR_7503_001_002,AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.PV)MOV(400.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.LoAlarmSP)MOV(30.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.LoFaultSP)MOV(100.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.LoAlarmLE),OTU(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.HasHiAlarm),XIO(Pump_Active_1_Hour)XIC(FS_7503_001_ALI)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.HasFaultWin),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[7503-FR-001/002 Output Unpacking: Maps outputs to FR_7503_001_002_VAL, _ALL, _ALLI, _ALH, _ALHI, _FRUP, _OC, _SC.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.Val,FR_7503_001_002_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.ALL)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.ALLI)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.ALH)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.ALHI)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.FRUP)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.OC)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_001_002.SC)OTE(FR_7503_001_002_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Spare Analog Input Channel 21 Setup: Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(SpareAI_21,AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.PV)MOV(400.0,AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.LoAlarmSP)MOV(30.0,AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.LoFaultSP)MOV(100.0,AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.LoAlarmLE),OTL(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.HasHiAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.HasFaultWin),XIC(SpareAI_21_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Spare Analog Input Channel 21 Output Unpacking: Maps outputs to SpareAI_21_VAL, _ALL, _ALLI, _ALH, _ALHI, _FRUP, _OC, _SC.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.Val,SpareAI_21_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.ALL)OTE(SpareAI_21_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.ALLI)OTE(SpareAI_21_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.ALH)OTE(SpareAI_21_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.ALHI)OTE(SpareAI_21_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.FRUP)OTE(SpareAI_21_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.OC)OTE(SpareAI_21_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_SpareAI_21.SC)OTE(SpareAI_21_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Foam Deluge Release Inside Local CP (7503-FR-003): Discharge pressure sensor inside local control panel (TB-03: 19). High Alarm = 30.0 PSI. Low Alarm disabled (LoAlarmSP = 400.0). Interlocked with deluge flow and pump run timer. Calls AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(FR_7503_003,AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.PV)MOV(400.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.LoAlarmSP)MOV(30.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.HiAlarmSP)MOV(-10.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.LoFaultSP)MOV(100.0,AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.HiFaultSP)[OTU(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.LoAlarmLE),OTU(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.HasLoAlarm),OTL(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.HasHiAlarm),XIO(Pump_Active_1_Hour)XIC(FS_7503_001_ALI)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.AllowHiLatch),OTU(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.HasFaultWin),XIC(FR_7503_003_INH)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.Inhibit),XIC(System_Reset)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.SystemReset),XIC(System_AnyActions)OTE(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.AnyActions)]AOI_AI_Channel(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[7503-FR-003 Output Unpacking: Maps outputs to FR_7503_003_VAL, _ALL, _ALLI, _ALH, _ALHI, _FRUP, _OC, _SC. ALHI triggers emergency shutdown and booster pump trips.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  MOV(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.Val,FR_7503_003_VAL)[XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.ALL)OTE(FR_7503_003_ALL),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.ALLI)OTE(FR_7503_003_ALLI),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.ALH)OTE(FR_7503_003_ALH),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.ALHI)OTE(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.FRUP)OTE(FR_7503_003_FRUP),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.OC)OTE(FR_7503_003_OC),XIC(AI_Inst_FR_7503_003.SC)OTE(FR_7503_003_SC)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Vote_1" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Vote_1 (Sensor Voting Logic & Supervisory Aggregation)
Executes 1oo2, 2oo2 voting across gas detector zones. Aggregates all active channel maintenance inhibits into 'Voting_All_Inhibits' and all channel hardware wire-break / open/short circuit faults into 'Voting_All_Faults' for HMI and supervisory panel indication.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Common Low Combustible Gas Voting (1oo10 OR Matrix): Evaluates uninhibited low alarm bits DG_7404_001_ALLI through DG_7404_010_ALLI in an OR configuration. If ANY single gas detector reaches 20% LEL, Voting_DG_7404_ALLI turns ON to activate local warning beacons.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(DG_7404_001_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_002_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_003_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_004_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_005_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_006_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_007_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_008_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_009_ALLI),XIC(DG_7404_010_ALLI)]OTE(Voting_DG_7404_ALLI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Common High Combustible Gas Voting (1oo10 OR Matrix): Evaluates uninhibited high alarm bits DG_7404_001_ALHI through DG_7404_010_ALHI in an OR configuration. If ANY single gas detector reaches 30% LEL, Voting_DG_7404_ALHI turns ON to initiate ESD trips in CE_LOG.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(DG_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_003_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_004_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_005_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_006_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_007_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_008_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_009_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_010_ALHI)]OTE(Voting_DG_7404_ALHI);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Master Channel Maintenance Inhibit Aggregation (Supervisory Inhibit Bus): Evaluates every individual channel manual inhibit switch (_INH) across all 32 discrete inputs and 24 analog channels. If ANY channel is bypassed for calibration or maintenance, Voting_All_Inhibits turns ON. Drives the white panel door inhibit LED (LAMP_CR6) and alerts control room operators via HMI.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(ZSH_6401_001_INH),XIC(ZSL_6401_001_INH),XIC(FS_7503_001_INH),XIC(LS_7503_001_INH),XIC(LS_7503_002_INH),XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_INH),XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_INH),XIC(SpareDI_08_INH),XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_INH),XIC(ESDV_6401_001_INH),XIC(SpareDI_11_INH),XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_INH),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_INH),XIC(SpareDI_14_INH),XIC(SpareDI_15_INH),XIC(SpareDI_16_INH),XIC(SpareDI_17_INH),XIC(SpareDI_18_INH),XIC(SpareDI_19_INH),XIC(SpareDI_20_INH),XIC(SpareDI_21_INH),XIC(SpareDI_22_INH),XIC(SpareDI_23_INH),XIC(SpareDI_24_INH),XIC(SpareDI_25_INH),XIC(SpareDI_26_INH),XIC(SpareDI_27_INH),XIC(SpareDI_28_INH),XIC(SpareDI_29_INH),XIC(SpareDI_30_INH),XIC(SpareDI_31_INH),XIC(SpareDI_32_INH),XIC(DG_7404_001_INH),XIC(DG_7404_002_INH),XIC(DG_7404_003_INH),XIC(DG_7404_004_INH),XIC(DG_7404_005_INH),XIC(DG_7404_006_INH),XIC(DG_7404_007_INH),XIC(DG_7404_008_INH),XIC(DG_7404_009_INH),XIC(DG_7404_010_INH),XIC(DG_7404_011R_INH),XIC(DF_7404_001_INH),XIC(DF_7404_002_INH),XIC(SpareAI_15_INH),XIC(SpareAI_16_INH),XIC(PST_7002_001_INH),XIC(PST_6401_001_INH),XIC(PST_7503_001_INH),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_INH),XIC(SpareAI_21_INH),XIC(FR_7503_003_INH),XIC(SpareAI_23_INH),XIC(SpareAI_24_INH)]OTE(Voting_All_Inhibits);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Master Hardware Fault & Wire-Break Aggregation (Supervisory Trouble Bus): Evaluates all open-circuit (_OC), short-circuit (_SC), and optical beam fault (_FLT1) flags across all channels. If ANY loop experiences wire-break (<3.6mA), short circuit (>21mA), or beam misalignment, Voting_All_Faults turns ON. Drives the amber panel door fault LED (LAMP_CR5) and PLC trouble annunciator.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(ZSH_6401_001_OC),XIC(ZSL_6401_001_OC),XIC(FS_7503_001_OC),XIC(LS_7503_001_OC),XIC(LS_7503_002_OC),XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_OC),XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_OC),XIC(SpareDI_08_OC),XIC(Pump_B_Inhibited_OC),XIC(ESDV_6401_001_OC),XIC(SpareDI_11_OC),XIC(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_OC),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_OC),XIC(SpareDI_14_OC),XIC(SpareDI_15_OC),XIC(SpareDI_16_OC),XIC(SpareDI_17_OC),XIC(SpareDI_18_OC),XIC(SpareDI_19_OC),XIC(SpareDI_20_OC),XIC(SpareDI_21_OC),XIC(SpareDI_22_OC),XIC(SpareDI_23_OC),XIC(SpareDI_24_OC),XIC(SpareDI_25_OC),XIC(SpareDI_26_OC),XIC(SpareDI_27_OC),XIC(SpareDI_28_OC),XIC(SpareDI_29_OC),XIC(SpareDI_30_OC),XIC(SpareDI_31_OC),XIC(SpareDI_32_OC),XIC(DG_7404_001_OC),XIC(DG_7404_001_SC),XIC(DG_7404_002_OC),XIC(DG_7404_002_SC),XIC(DG_7404_003_OC),XIC(DG_7404_003_SC),XIC(DG_7404_004_OC),XIC(DG_7404_004_SC),XIC(DG_7404_005_OC),XIC(DG_7404_005_SC),XIC(DG_7404_006_OC),XIC(DG_7404_006_SC),XIC(DG_7404_007_OC),XIC(DG_7404_007_SC),XIC(DG_7404_008_OC),XIC(DG_7404_008_SC),XIC(DG_7404_009_OC),XIC(DG_7404_009_SC),XIC(DG_7404_010_OC),XIC(DG_7404_010_SC),XIC(SpareAI_11_OC),XIC(SpareAI_11_SC),XIC(DF_7404_001_OC),XIC(DF_7404_001_SC),XIC(DF_7404_002_OC),XIC(DF_7404_002_SC),XIC(DG_7404_011R_OC),XIC(DG_7404_011R_SC),XIC(SpareAI_15_OC),XIC(SpareAI_15_SC),XIC(SpareAI_16_OC),XIC(SpareAI_16_SC),XIC(PST_7002_001_OC),XIC(PST_7002_001_SC),XIC(PST_6401_001_OC),XIC(PST_6401_001_SC),XIC(PST_7503_001_OC),XIC(PST_7503_001_SC),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_OC),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_SC),XIC(SpareAI_21_OC),XIC(SpareAI_21_SC),XIC(FR_7503_003_OC),XIC(FR_7503_003_SC),XIC(SpareAI_23_OC),XIC(SpareAI_23_SC),XIC(SpareAI_24_OC),XIC(SpareAI_24_SC),XIC(DG_7404_011R_FLT1)]OTE(Voting_All_Faults);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Logic (Master Cause & Effect Matrix & System Clocks)
Generates 1.0-second flasher pulses and 1.0-minute watchdog clocks. Executes the 120-second detector warm-up delay timer (TMR_C_E_Delay), evaluates master System_Reset from panel PB E11 and HMI touch button, performs controller minor fault logging (GSV/SSV), and dispatches CE_LOG.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[1.0-Second Free-Running Clock Generator: 1000 ms self-resetting on-delay timer (TMR_T_SEC). Provides master timebase for alarm flasher frequencies and pulsed outputs.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(TMR_T_SEC.DN)TON(TMR_T_SEC,1000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[1.0-Second Square Wave Pulse Generator: Compares timer accumulator TMR_T_SEC.ACC < 500 ms. Produces clean 50% duty cycle square wave (500 ms ON / 500 ms OFF) in tag 'T_SEC_PULSE' to flash panel lamps.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  LES(TMR_T_SEC.ACC,500)OTE(T_SEC_PULSE);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[1.0-Minute Free-Running Clock Generator: 60,000 ms self-resetting timer (TMR_T_MIN). Provides master timebase for hourly accumulation and long-term watchdogs.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(TMR_T_MIN.DN)TON(TMR_T_MIN,60000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[1.0-Minute Square Wave Pulse Generator: Compares TMR_T_MIN.ACC < 30,000 ms. Produces 30 seconds ON / 30 seconds OFF pulse in tag 'T_MIN_PULSE'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  LES(TMR_T_MIN.ACC,30000)OTE(T_MIN_PULSE);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Master System Reset Consolidation: Single deterministic rung driving 'System_Reset'. Activated by: (1) Physical panel door pushbutton E11 System_Reset_PB (TB-01: 21-22), (2) PanelView HMI touch reset button System_Reset_HMI, (3) Automatic power-up startup pulse System_Reset_Startup, or (4) First program scan S:FS. Resets all latched alarm registers and clears fault tables.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(System_Reset_PB),XIC(System_Reset_HMI),XIC(System_Reset_Startup),XIC(S:FS)]OTE(System_Reset);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[HMI Touch Reset Pulse-Stretching Timer: 5000 ms on-delay timer (TMR_HMI_Reset). When an operator presses Reset on the HMI screen, holds the reset state active for a guaranteed 5.0 seconds so all remote network racks, voting blocks, and debounce timers process the reset transition reliably.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(System_Reset_HMI)TON(TMR_HMI_Reset,5000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[HMI Reset Self-Clearing Logic: When the 5.0-second HMI timer completes (TMR_HMI_Reset.DN), automatically unlatches System_Reset_HMI and resets the timer, preventing operators from leaving the system in perpetual reset.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_HMI_Reset.DN)[OTU(System_Reset_HMI),RES(TMR_HMI_Reset)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ControlLogix Minor Fault Table Read (GSV): Reads controller minor fault bitmask from System Object 'FaultLog' into tag 'Sys_MinorFaultBits'. Replaces legacy GE Fanuc system status bits #LOW_BAT, #LOS_IOM, and #HRD_FLT.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  GSV(FaultLog,,MinorFaultBits,Sys_MinorFaultBits);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Battery / Energy Storage Status Monitoring: Evaluates MinorFaultBits.10 to detect real-time clock energy storage / battery low voltage. Drives tag 'SYS_LOW_BAT'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.10)OTE(SYS_LOW_BAT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[I/O Backplane Communication Fault Monitoring: Evaluates MinorFaultBits.3 to detect lost connection to any 1756 I/O chassis module. Drives tag 'SYS_LOS_IOM'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.3)OTE(SYS_LOS_IOM);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Controller Processor / Watchdog Fault Monitoring: Evaluates MinorFaultBits.4 (program execution fault) and MinorFaultBits.6 (watchdog timer expiration). Drives tag 'SYS_HRD_FLT'.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.4),XIC(Sys_MinorFaultBits.6)]OTE(SYS_HRD_FLT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Controller Fault Table Clear (SSV): Upon master System_Reset, writes zero (Sys_FaultClearZero) into FaultLog MinorFaultBits using SSV instruction. Replaces legacy GE Fanuc SVC_REQ function 14 (Clear I/O Fault Table).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(System_Reset)SSV(FaultLog,,MinorFaultBits,Sys_FaultClearZero);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Detector Power-Up Burn-In Warm-Up Timer: 120,000 ms (120 seconds / 2 minutes) on-delay timer (TMR_C_E_Delay). Prevents false trips: combustible catalytic bead gas detectors and optical flame detectors require up to 2 minutes to thermally stabilize after power restoration. Inhibits Cause & Effect trips during this stabilization window.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  TON(TMR_C_E_Delay,120000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Detector Warm-Up Complete Interlock Flag: When 120-second timer completes (TMR_C_E_Delay.DN), energizes tag 'T00002', unlocking the Cause & Effect shutdown matrix for active safety protection.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_C_E_Delay.DN)OTE(T00002);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pre-Arming Auto-Reset Pulse: At 118 seconds (2.0 seconds before the 120s warm-up completes), generates a 2-second pulse on 'System_Reset_Startup' to clear any spurious alarm latches that occurred during detector boot-up.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  GEQ(TMR_C_E_Delay.ACC,118000)XIO(TMR_C_E_Delay.DN)OTE(System_Reset_Startup);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Cause & Effect Matrix Routine Execution Dispatcher: When detector warm-up is complete (XIC T00002), calls subroutine 'CE_LOG' to evaluate plant shutdown interlocks.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(T00002)JSR(CE_LOG,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Acoustic Alarm & Siren Routine Dispatcher: Calls subroutine 'Sound' on all scans except first scan (XIO S:FS) to evaluate alarm edge triggers and siren cadences.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(S:FS)JSR(Sound,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="CE_LOG" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: CE_LOG (Cause & Effect Shutdown Matrix & Pump Sequencing)
Executes the core safety interlocks: process pump shutdown (PumpShutdown), fuel gas valve isolation (EY_6401_001_002), electrical booster pump trips (P2100/P2200, P3600/P3700), and diesel pump B automatic 3-cycle cranking sequence with deluge pressure feedback and 1-hour pump run limiting.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Main Process Pumps & Booster Feeders Emergency Shutdown Matrix: Evaluates confirmed fire and gas shutdown causes: (1) High combustible gas voting Voting_DG_7404_ALHI, (2) Perimeter open-path high gas DG_7404_011R_ALHI, (3) Foam release in control room FR_7503_003_ALHI, (4) Optical flame detector Zone 1 DF_7404_001_ALHI, (5) Fuel gas overpressure PST_6401_001_ALHI, (6) Optical flame detector Zone 2 DF_7404_002_ALHI, (7) ESD valve closed limit ZSL_6401_001_ALI, (8) Foam release outside FR_7503_001_002_ALHI, or (9) Manual field ESD pushbutton ESDV_6401_001_ALI. Simultaneously drives trip internal coils: P2100_P2200_INT (Oil Booster Feeder), P3600_P3700_INT (Water Booster Feeder), and PumpShutdown_INT (Process Pumps Trip).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(Voting_DG_7404_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_011R_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(PST_6401_001_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(ZSL_6401_001_ALI),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI),XIC(ESDV_6401_001_ALI)][OTE(P2100_P2200_INT),OTE(P3600_P3700_INT),OTE(PumpShutdown_INT)];
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Emergency Shut-Off Valve Isolation Matrix: Trips internal isolation command EY_6401_001_002_INT upon: high combustible gas, open path gas trip, foam discharge, flame detection in Zone 1/2, or fuel gas line overpressure. De-energizes fuel gas solenoids.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(Voting_DG_7404_ALHI),XIC(DG_7404_011R_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(PST_6401_001_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI)]OTE(EY_6401_001_002_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Fire Pump A Automatic Start Command: Initiates Electric Pump A (PUMP_A_INT) upon confirmed fire alarm (Zone 1 flame DF_7404_001, Zone 2 flame DF_7404_002, or foam discharge). Interlocked with deluge flow switch FS_7503_001_ALI, unlatched by master System_Reset, and automatically inhibited if the 1-hour pump active limit (Pump_Active_1_Hour) has been reached.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(DF_7404_001_ALHI),XIC(DF_7404_002_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI),XIC(FR_7503_003_ALHI),XIC(PUMP_A_INT)]XIC(FS_7503_001_ALI)XIO(System_Reset)XIO(Pump_Active_1_Hour)OTE(PUMP_A_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Pump A Hourly Operation Counter: Increments counter CTR_Pump_A_Hour on every 1-second pulse (T_SEC_PULSE) while Pump A is actively running (PUMP_A_INT). Preset = 3600 counts (3600 seconds = 1.0 hour).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PUMP_A_INT)XIC(T_SEC_PULSE)CTU(CTR_Pump_A_Hour,3600,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Pump A 1-Hour Run Limit Reached Flag: Driven by counter done bit CTR_Pump_A_Hour.DN. Sets tag 'Pump_Active_1_Hour' to prevent pump motor burn-out and prevent total depletion of the firewater storage tank.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(CTR_Pump_A_Hour.DN)OTE(Pump_Active_1_Hour);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump Operation Counter Reset Logic: Resets counter CTR_Pump_A_Hour when deluge flow stops (XIO FS_7503_001_ALI), when master System_Reset is pressed, or when the 1-hour run limit is acknowledged.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIO(FS_7503_001_ALI),XIC(System_Reset),XIC(Pump_Active_1_Hour)]RES(CTR_Pump_A_Hour);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Standby Diesel Pump B Auto-Start 30-Second Evaluation Timer: When Electric Pump A is commanded to start (PUMP_A_INT), timer TMR_T00003 runs for 30,000 ms (30 seconds). If deluge line pressure (PST_7503_001_ALHI) is NOT established within 30 seconds, this timer completes to automatically trigger standby Diesel Pump B!]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PUMP_A_INT)TON(TMR_T00003,30000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Standby Evaluation Timer Reset: Resets timer TMR_T00003 once deluge line pressure is verified healthy (PST_7503_001_ALHI = 1) or when Electric Pump A is stopped.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(PST_7503_001_ALHI),XIO(PUMP_A_INT)]RES(TMR_T00003);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Cranking Cycle 1 - Crank Pulse: 2000 ms (2.0 seconds) timer TMR_T00004. Provides the first 2-second starter motor crank pulse to the Clarke / Murphy diesel engine.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_T00003.DN)TON(TMR_T00004,2000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Cranking Cycle 1 - Rest Interval: 60,000 ms (60 seconds) timer TMR_T00005. Allows starter motor and battery bank to cool down after Crank 1 before attempting Crank 2.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_T00004.DN)TON(TMR_T00005,60000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Cranking Cycle 2 - Crank Pulse: 2000 ms (2.0 seconds) timer TMR_T00006. Provides the second 2-second starter motor crank pulse.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_T00005.DN)TON(TMR_T00006,2000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Cranking Cycle 2 - Rest Interval: 60,000 ms (60 seconds) timer TMR_T00007. Second 60-second starter rest interval.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_T00006.DN)TON(TMR_T00007,60000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Cranking Cycle 3 - Crank Pulse: 2000 ms (2.0 seconds) timer TMR_T00008. Provides the third and final 2-second starter motor crank pulse.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_T00007.DN)TON(TMR_T00008,2000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Master Starter Solenoid Command: Drives PUMP_B_START_INT during active crank windows: Crank 1 (T00003.DN and NOT T00004.DN), Crank 2 (T00005.DN and NOT T00006.DN), or Crank 3 (T00007.DN and NOT T00008.DN).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(TMR_T00003.DN)XIO(TMR_T00004.DN),XIC(TMR_T00005.DN)XIO(TMR_T00006.DN),XIC(TMR_T00007.DN)XIO(TMR_T00008.DN)]OTE(PUMP_B_START_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Deluge Failure to Release Watchdog Timer: 60,000 ms (60 seconds) timer TMR_DelugeFail. Starts after Diesel Pump B has exhausted all 3 crank attempts (TMR_T00008.DN).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_T00008.DN)TON(TMR_DelugeFail,60000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Deluge System Failed to Release Critical Alarm: Driven by timer done bit TMR_DelugeFail.DN. Asserts tag 'DelugeFailedToRelease' if deluge line pressure is still not achieved after all crank cycles.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_DelugeFail.DN)OTE(DelugeFailedToRelease);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Deluge Failure Timer Reset: Resets timer TMR_DelugeFail once deluge pressure is verified (PST_7503_001_ALHI).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(PST_7503_001_ALHI),XIO(TMR_T00008.DN)]RES(TMR_DelugeFail);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="17" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Auto-Stop 2-Second Confirmation Timer: 2000 ms timer TMR_T00009. Confirms that all fire flame alarms and foam release commands have cleared before stopping the diesel pump.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(DF_7404_001_ALHI)XIO(DF_7404_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_003_ALHI)TON(TMR_T00009,2000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="18" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Stop Solenoid Command: Drives PUMP_B_STOP_INT to energize the engine fuel rack stop solenoid when deluge flow switch opens (no firewater demand) and all fire alarms have cleared.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIO(FS_7503_001_ALI),XIO(DF_7404_001_ALHI)XIO(DF_7404_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_001_002_ALHI)XIO(FR_7503_003_ALHI)XIO(TMR_T00009.DN)]OTE(PUMP_B_STOP_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="19" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Closed Panel LED Logic: When fuel gas shut-off valve is closed (ZSL_6401_001_ALI), drives internal indicator bit Tag_DO_13_INT to illuminate panel LED L14.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ZSL_6401_001_ALI)OTE(Tag_DO_13_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="20" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Open Panel LED Logic: When fuel gas shut-off valve is open (ZSH_6401_001_ALI), drives internal indicator bit Tag_DO_12_INT to illuminate panel LED L15.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(ZSH_6401_001_ALI)OTE(Tag_DO_12_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="21" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Low Air Pressure Panel LED Logic: When pneumatic air accumulator pressure drops below 50 PSI (PST_7002_001_ALLI), drives internal indicator bit Tag_DO_14_INT to illuminate low air warning LED.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PST_7002_001_ALLI)OTE(Tag_DO_14_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="22" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[System First-Up Action One-Shot Pulse: One-shot rising edge instruction ONS(OS_AnyActions) produces a 1-scan pulse on 'System_AnyActions' whenever an ESD trip, pump start, or valve closure is initiated. Triggers First-Out event traps.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(P2100_P2200_INT),XIC(EY_6401_001_002_INT),XIC(PUMP_A_INT),XIC(PUMP_B_START_INT)]ONS(OS_AnyActions)OTE(System_AnyActions);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Sound" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Sound (Acoustic Siren Cadence, Strobe Flasher & Alarm Mute)
Detects rising edge alarm events via one-shots, latches acoustic horns and visual beacons, and processes panel door Mute pushbutton E12 (Mute_Alm_PB) to allow operators to silence acoustic horns during an emergency while maintaining flashing beacons and active safety trip interlocks.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-001 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound01.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_001_ALH)ONS(System_Sound01_OS)OTE(System_Sound01);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-001 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound02.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_001_ALL)ONS(System_Sound02_OS)OTE(System_Sound02);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-002 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound03.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_002_ALH)ONS(System_Sound03_OS)OTE(System_Sound03);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-002 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound04.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_002_ALL)ONS(System_Sound04_OS)OTE(System_Sound04);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-003 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound05.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_003_ALH)ONS(System_Sound05_OS)OTE(System_Sound05);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-003 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound06.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_003_ALL)ONS(System_Sound06_OS)OTE(System_Sound06);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-004 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound07.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_004_ALH)ONS(System_Sound07_OS)OTE(System_Sound07);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-004 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound08.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_004_ALL)ONS(System_Sound08_OS)OTE(System_Sound08);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-005 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound09.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_005_ALH)ONS(System_Sound09_OS)OTE(System_Sound09);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-005 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound10.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_005_ALL)ONS(System_Sound10_OS)OTE(System_Sound10);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-006 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound11.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_006_ALH)ONS(System_Sound11_OS)OTE(System_Sound11);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-006 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound12.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_006_ALL)ONS(System_Sound12_OS)OTE(System_Sound12);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-007 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound13.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_007_ALH)ONS(System_Sound13_OS)OTE(System_Sound13);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-007 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound14.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_007_ALL)ONS(System_Sound14_OS)OTE(System_Sound14);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-008 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound15.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_008_ALH)ONS(System_Sound15_OS)OTE(System_Sound15);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-008 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound16.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_008_ALL)ONS(System_Sound16_OS)OTE(System_Sound16);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-009 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound17.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_009_ALH)ONS(System_Sound17_OS)OTE(System_Sound17);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="17" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-009 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound18.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_009_ALL)ONS(System_Sound18_OS)OTE(System_Sound18);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="18" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-010 High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound19.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_010_ALH)ONS(System_Sound19_OS)OTE(System_Sound19);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="19" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Gas Detector 7404-DG-010 Low Alarm (ALL) -> One-shot System_Sound20.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_010_ALL)ONS(System_Sound20_OS)OTE(System_Sound20);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="20" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Rising Edge Detection: Open Path Gas Detector 7404-DG-011R High Alarm (ALH) -> One-shot System_Sound21.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(DG_7404_011R_ALH)ONS(System_Sound21_OS)OTE(System_Sound21);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
