<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(System_Reset),XIC(System_Mute)]OTU(SA_7404_001_002_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="43" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[PLC Fault Annunciator Silence / Unlatch: Unlatches PLC_Fault_INT upon System_Reset or System_Mute.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(System_Reset),XIC(System_Mute)]OTU(PLC_Fault_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="44" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Alarm Mute Pushbutton Processing: Reads physical push button E12 on panel door Mute_Alm_PB (TB-01: 23-24). Drives 'System_Mute' to silence acoustic sirens without resetting visual beacons or emergency trip interlocks, enabling personnel communication during an active field incident.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Mute_Alm_PB)OTE(System_Mute);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Output" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Output (Master Output Execution Dispatcher)
Dispatches final output conditioning subroutines: Shutdow (ESD trips), Protect (equipment safeguarding), Indicat (panel lamps), Loc_Al (local annunciator), FLT_1 (fault watchdogs), and IO_Mapping_Out (writes to physical Slot 8 1756-OB32 module).]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Emergency Shutdown Outputs Dispatcher: Calls 'Shutdow' to drive fail-safe de-energize to trip outputs.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(Shutdow,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Equipment Safeguarding Outputs Dispatcher: Calls 'Protect' to condition pump run pulses and interlocks.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(Protect,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Panel LED Pilot Lamps Dispatcher: Calls 'Indicat' to drive door-mounted status lamps.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(Indicat,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Local Panel Alarm Dispatcher: Calls 'Loc_Al' to drive local panel horn and strobe beacons.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(Loc_Al,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[System Diagnostic Watchdog Dispatcher: Calls 'FLT_1' to update pump pulse output commands.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(FLT_1,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Physical Backplane Output Write: Calls 'IO_Mapping_Out' to transfer all commands to Slot 8 1756-OB32 module.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  JSR(IO_Mapping_Out,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Shutdow" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Shutdow (Emergency Shutdown Fail-Safe Outputs)
Drives critical ESD outputs using Fail-Safe Active-Low (De-energize to Trip) logic: PumpShutdown, EY_6401_001_002, P2100_P2200, and P3600_P3700. In safe state, coils are energized (1); upon fire/gas confirmation or power loss, coils de-energize (0) to bring the facility to a safe stop.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Fuel Gas Emergency Shut-Off Valves (6401-EY-001/002) - Fail-Safe Active-Low: In normal healthy operating state, internal trip coil EY_6401_001_002_INT is OFF (0), so XIO evaluates TRUE and physical output EY_6401_001_002 is ENERGIZED (1), holding fuel gas valves open. Upon fire/gas emergency trip, internal coil energizes (1), XIO opens, and the output DE-ENERGIZES (0) to spring-close the fuel gas valves. Held energized if master maintenance inhibit INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI is active.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIO(EY_6401_001_002_INT)XIC(EY_6401_001_002_MT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(EY_6401_001_002);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Main Process Pumps Emergency Shutdown (PumpShutdown) - Fail-Safe Active-Low: Normal state: output is ENERGIZED (1) holding pump MCC permissive contact closed. Trip state: output DE-ENERGIZES (0) to instantly trip all main process pump motors (TB-08: 01-02). Loss of control power causes immediate safe shutdown.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIO(PumpShutdown_INT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(PumpShutdown);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Oil Booster Pumps Feeder EDB1 Trip (P2100_P2200) - Fail-Safe Active-Low: Normal state: output is ENERGIZED (1). Trip state: output DE-ENERGIZES (0) to shunt-trip booster pump breakers (TB-08: 17-18).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIO(P2100_P2200_INT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(P2100_P2200);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Water Booster Pumps Feeder EDB2 Trip (P3600_P3700) - Fail-Safe Active-Low: Normal state: output is ENERGIZED (1). Trip state: output DE-ENERGIZES (0) to shunt-trip booster pump breakers (TB-08: 19-20).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIO(P3600_P3700_INT),XIC(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)]OTE(P3600_P3700);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Protect" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Protect (Pump Safeguarding, Pulse Outputs & Disagree Diagnostics)
Generates 1.5-second start pulses for fire pumps, enforces maintenance inhibit interlocks (INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS, INHIBIT_FOAM_REL), and executes 70-second pump start disagree watchdog timers to detect pump contactor failure or open circuit wiring.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Fire Pump A Continuous Run Command: Interlocked with foam release inhibit INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI and master output inhibit INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI. Drives physical output PUMP_A (TB-08: 09-10).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PUMP_A_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)XIO(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)OTE(PUMP_A);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Start Pilot Command: Interlocked with foam inhibit and master inhibit. Drives physical output PUMP_B_START (TB-08: 13-14).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PUMP_B_START_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)XIO(INHIBIT_ALL_OUTPUTS_ALI)OTE(PUMP_B_START);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Fire Pump B Stop Command: Drives physical output PUMP_B_STOP (TB-08: 15-16) to energize the fuel rack stop solenoid.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PUMP_B_STOP_INT)OTE(PUMP_B_STOP);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump A Pulse Reset: Resets timer TMR_Pump_Timer11 when 1-minute pulse clock T_MIN_PULSE is low.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(T_MIN_PULSE)RES(TMR_Pump_Timer11);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump A Pulse On-Delay Timer: 28,000 ms timer generating the pulse duration for Pump A remote start.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(T00002)XIC(T_MIN_PULSE)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer11,28000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump A Pulse Timer Output Flag: Sets T00013 when timer completes.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer11.DN)OTE(T00013);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Pump A Momentary Start Pulse Generator: Drives internal pulse command Pump_A_PulsOut_INT to deliver a 1.5-second pulse to the MCC starter relay.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(T00013)XIC(T00002),XIC(PUMP_A)]OTE(Pump_A_PulsOut_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump A Disagree Watchdog Reset: Resets 70-second timer TMR_Pump_Timer9 when pump run feedback Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI is received.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(Pump_A_PulsIn_ALI),XIC(PUMP_A_INT)]RES(TMR_Pump_Timer9);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump A Start Disagree Timer: 70,000 ms (70 seconds) watchdog timer TMR_Pump_Timer9.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(T00002)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer9,70000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Electric Pump A Start Failure / Disagree Alarm: If Pump A was commanded to start but feedback is NOT received within 70 seconds, sets PUMP_A_OC (Pump A Contactor Open Circuit / Run Disagree Fault).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer9.DN)OTE(PUMP_A_OC);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump B Pulse Reset: Resets timer TMR_Pump_Timer12 on 1-minute clock low.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIO(T_MIN_PULSE)RES(TMR_Pump_Timer12);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump B Pulse On-Delay Timer: 28,000 ms timer for Diesel Pump B start pulse.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(T00002)XIC(T_MIN_PULSE)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer12,28000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump B Pulse Timer Output Flag: Sets T00014 when timer completes.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer12.DN)OTE(T00014);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="13" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Momentary Start Pulse Generator: Drives internal pulse command Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT to deliver a start crank pulse to the Murphy engine panel.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  [XIC(T00014)XIC(T00002),XIC(PUMP_B_START)]OTE(Pump_B_Start_PulsOut_INT);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="14" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump B Disagree Watchdog Reset: Resets 70-second timer TMR_Pump_Timer10 when start feedback Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI is received.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Pump_B_Start_PulsIn_ALI)RES(TMR_Pump_Timer10);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="15" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Pump B Start Disagree Timer: 70,000 ms (70 seconds) watchdog timer TMR_Pump_Timer10.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(T00002)TON(TMR_Pump_Timer10,70000,0);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="16" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Diesel Pump B Start Failure / Disagree Alarm: If Pump B was cranked but engine run feedback is NOT received within 70 seconds, sets PUMP_B_START_OC (Diesel Engine Crank Disagree Fault).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(TMR_Pump_Timer10.DN)OTE(PUMP_B_START_OC);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Indicat" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Indicat (Panel Door LED Pilot Lamp Drivers)
Drives status pilot lamps on the enclosure door: ESDV closed status (Tag_DO_13), ESDV open status (Tag_DO_12), and ESDV low pneumatic air pressure warning (Tag_DO_14).]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Closed Panel LED Driver: Passes Tag_DO_13_INT to physical output Tag_DO_13 to light LED L14 (TB-08: 23-24).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Tag_DO_13_INT)OTE(Tag_DO_13);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Open Panel LED Driver: Passes Tag_DO_12_INT to physical output Tag_DO_12 to light LED L15 (TB-08: 25-26).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Tag_DO_12_INT)OTE(Tag_DO_12);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[ESDV Low Air Pressure LED Driver: Passes Tag_DO_14_INT to physical output Tag_DO_14 to light LED L16 (TB-08: 27-28).]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Tag_DO_14_INT)OTE(Tag_DO_14);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Loc_Al" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: Loc_Al (Local Panel Annunciator, Siren & Horn Arbitration)
Arbitrates local panel annunciator buzzer, main acoustic horn (SA_7404_001_002), and visual strobe (Tag_DO_15), interlocked with maintenance foam inhibit.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Acoustic Alarm Siren Output: Passes internal horn command SA_7404_001_002_INT to physical output SA_7404_001_002 (TB-08: 05-06), suppressed when maintenance foam inhibit INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI is active.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(SA_7404_001_002_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)OTE(SA_7404_001_002);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[Optical Strobe Flasher Output: Passes internal beacon command Tag_DO_15_INT to physical output Tag_DO_15 (TB-08: 45-46), suppressed when foam inhibit is active.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(Tag_DO_15_INT)XIO(INHIBIT_FOAM_REL_ALI)OTE(Tag_DO_15);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment>
<![CDATA[PLC System Health Watchdog Output (Fail-Safe): Drives physical output PLC_Fault (TB-08: 21-22). Normally ENERGIZED (1) when system is healthy; de-energizes (0) upon fatal hardware failure, rack fault, or power loss.]]>
                </Comment>
                <Text>
<![CDATA[
                  XIC(PLC_Fault_INT)XIO(Tag_DO_15)OTE(PLC_Fault);
                ]]>
                </Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="FLT_1" Type="RLL">
            <Description>
<![CDATA[Subroutine: FLT_1 (System Fault Annunciation & Output Watchdogs)
Conditions pulse output commands for Electric Pump A and Diesel Pump B, ensuring deterministic signal duration to motor control center (MCC) starter relays.]]>
            </Description>
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
